### Kali Linux (64-bit)
- Guest OS: Kali Linux (64-bit)
- VM purpose:
  - Penetration testing
  - Security experiments
  - Network scanning and monitoring
- Resource Allocation:
  - CPUs: 2
  - Memory: 2 GB
  - Storage: 20 GB VDI (dynamically allocated)
- Why VirtualBox:
  - Lightweight Linux distribution
  - Ideal for testing without affecting host OS
  - Easy snapshotting for experiments
- Limitations:
  - Requires careful network configuration for lab isolation
  - Performance depends on host resources
  - Not intended for production workloads


## Virtual Machine 3
## Kali-Red01
- Guest OS: Red Hat Enterprise Linux (64-bit)
- VM purpose:
  - Linux server testing
  - Learning enterprise Linux commands and administration
  - Service hosting (web server, database)
- Resource Allocation:
  - CPUs: 2
  - Memory: 2 GB
  - Storage: 20 GB VDI (dynamically allocated)
- Why VirtualBox:
  - Cross-platform virtualization for Linux
  - Supports enterprise-level features for testing
  - Snapshots allow safe experimentation
- Limitations:
  - Host performance affects VM speed
  - Enterprise features may require subscription
  - Not designed for high availability


## Virtual Machine 4
## WIN11-Clint01 (64-bit)
- Guest OS: Windows 11 (64-bit)
- VM purpose:
  - General-purpose workstation
  - Testing software in isolated environment
  - Learning Windows features and settings
- Resource Allocation:
  - CPUs: 2
  - Memory: 4 GB
  - Storage: 30 GB VDI (dynamically allocated)
- Why VirtualBox:
  - Familiar Windows environment for testing
  - Allows safe experimentation without affecting host OS
- Limitations:
  - Higher RAM requirement than lightweight VMs
  - Performance depends on host resources
  - Not intended for production workloads
